  <section class="rich-lesson-section" data-g7-u06-l01 aria-label="Grade 7 Relationships between Quantities">
    <h3>Relationships between Quantities — Edulytiks</h3>
    <h4>Source-aligned focus</h4><p>Distinguish proportional from nonproportional relationships and identify useful unknown quantities. Use the existing lesson examples and activities while keeping diagrams and explanations explicit.</p>
    <h4>Practice connection</h4><p>Popcorn, entrance-fee, and toast contexts. Machine-scored Practice checks only closed numeric or symbolic subresults; representational reasoning remains teacher reviewed.</p>
    <h4>Cool-down — first-party Edulytiks assessment</h4><p>A theater charges 4.50 for a box plus 1.25 per topping. Write a rule for total cost, explain why it is not proportional to toppings, and find the cost for 6 toppings.</p>
    <p><strong>Teacher review:</strong> Check representation choice, algebraic reasoning, interpretation, and written justification. This Cool-down is independently authored.</p>
  </section>
}

